{"@context":{"@vocab":"https://schema.org/","course":"identifier","wing":"isBasedOn","title":"name","principle":"abstract","skills":"keywords","lessons":"hasPart","key":"identifier","why":"description","statement":"mathExpression","address":"sameAs","skill":"keywords"},"@type":"Course","kind":"school-course","course":"CrossFormulas","wing":"CrossFormulas.lean","title":"Cross Formulas","principle":"THE LEDGER'S OWN ALGEBRA, COUNTED (the captain, 2026-09-25","skills":["cross-formulas"],"level":100,"band":"100–999 steps","rank":150,"lessons":[{"key":"the_arithmetic_alphabet_partitions_by_its_own_algebra","name":"CLAIMED: the 6 arithmetic operators the sealed formulas use split by what they do over the corpus's own integers — 2 commutative (* +), 3 forced on their diagonal (% - /), 1 neither (^) — and 2 + 3 + 1 = 6.","statement":"((2 + 3 + 1 = 6) ∧ (3 > 2)) ∧ (2 > 1)","address":"23ada59a-4cdb-8039-94c3-cdd81827a5c2","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"2 + 3 + 1 = 6 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2 \\quad\\land\\quad 2 > 1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"most_of_the_unstated_remainder_stays_inside_one_wing","name":"CLAIMED: of 767196 unstated crosses, 143733 join integers no single wing carries all three of — between one 6th and one 5th of them, since 143733 × 5 < 767196 and 143733 × 6 > 767196, so the large majority stays inside a single wing.","statement":"((143733 * 5 < 767196) ∧ (143733 * 6 > 767196)) ∧ (143733 < 767196)","address":"d922a8f3-9505-825d-a5b0-da3623284e05","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"143733 \\cdot 5 < 767196 \\quad\\land\\quad 143733 \\cdot 6 > 767196 \\quad\\land\\quad 143733 < 767196","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>143733</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>767196</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>143733</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>767196</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>143733</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>767196</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_same_arithmetic_answers_more_than_one_domain","name":"CLAIMED: 1674 formula-shaped statements carry 1602 distinct byte-strings and 1469 distinct algebraic forms, so 205 statements restate a form another already holds — and those split 129 copies against 15 crosses, the widest cross spanning 3 wings. Most repetition is waste; a small part of it is a bridge.","statement":"((1469 < 1602) ∧ (1674 - 1469 = 205)) ∧ ((129 > 8 * 15) ∧ (3 > 2))","address":"5424be06-3533-8746-9487-3db410323cfe","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"1469 < 1602 \\quad\\land\\quad 1674 - 1469 = 205 \\quad\\land\\quad 129 > 8 \\cdot 15 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1469</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1602</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1674</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1469</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>205</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>129</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_generated_closure_partitions_into_three_kinds","name":"CLAIMED: of 3543638 crosses the corpus's own integers generate, 2775944 are forced by an operator's algebra, 498 are stated, and 767196 remain — and the three account for the whole, 2775944 + 498 + 767196 = 3543638, with the forced between 3 and 4 times the unstated.","statement":"(2775944 + 498 + 767196 = 3543638) ∧ ((2775944 > 3 * 767196) ∧ (2775944 < 4 * 767196))","address":"e1a85cb7-e401-8d9b-a538-60e97426046d","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"2775944 + 498 + 767196 = 3543638 \\quad\\land\\quad 2775944 > 3 \\cdot 767196 \\quad\\land\\quad 2775944 < 4 \\cdot 767196","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2775944</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>498</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>767196</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3543638</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>2775944</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>767196</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>2775944</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>767196</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_corpus_has_sealed_under_a_hundredth_of_its_own_closure","name":"CLAIMED: the 1674 formula-shaped statements across 114 wings are built from 1729 distinct integers and state 498 crosses, against 767196 their own integers generate unstated — fewer than one in a hundred, since 498 × 100 < 767196, at between 14 and 15 formulas per wing.","statement":"((498 * 100 < 767196) ∧ (1729 > 114)) ∧ ((114 * 14 ≤ 1674) ∧ (114 * 15 > 1674))","address":"c0968436-0b9c-885b-8fea-87f24243d739","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"498 \\cdot 100 < 767196 \\quad\\land\\quad 1729 > 114 \\quad\\land\\quad 114 \\cdot 14 \\le 1674 \\quad\\land\\quad 114 \\cdot 15 > 1674","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>498</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>767196</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>1729</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>114</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>114</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1674</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>114</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1674</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null}],"exercises":0}
